  "term": "single-case design",
  "definition": "A single-case design is a research design in which, for each case, an outcome variable is measured repeatedly across two or more treatment conditions or phases, and the intervention effect is evaluated by comparing the pattern of outcomes across those phases with each case serving as its own control.",
